MAJOR_VERSION=5
STANDARD_VERSION=3
RELEASE_VERSION=0
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=5
DESCRIPTION=KeyQuorum co-signed file delivery in the hosted shell. A tracked file now reaches its recipient only after both parties sign it: server file send -t <path> -user <name> checks the file in as a KeyQuorum revision, author-signs it and seals the payload and its history to the recipient's X25519 box key, the host announces a co-signature request, server file cosign <delivery> has the recipient sign the public offer, and only then does the host release the sealed letter, which the recipient decodes and verifies (server file open <delivery> retries after a destination conflict). The pipeline is shaped as an encoder (sender checkpoint), latent space (host: holds opaque letters it cannot open, routes announcements and parts, answers public key lookups from its account store), and decoder (recipient checkpoint), with each delivery an integrate-and-fire unit: verified signatures are spikes (REQUEST, OFFER, ANNOUNCE, COSIGN, RELEASE, ACK, logged in kq_spike), the host fires once at threshold 2 and is then refractory, and an unanswered delivery leaks after 24 h on the host's clock and its letter is deleted. The recipient applies threshold 3 (author signature, policy trust, its own co-author proof), refuses forked files until merged, replays and older revisions (.kqseen), and never overwrites an untracked file. New ASM primitives asm_mem_secure_zero and asm_mem_ct_equal (GAS x86-64, NASM, AArch64; the delivery SHA-256 compare now uses the constant-time one); accounts gain a password-sealed box key beside the signing key (created at the next login for older accounts, resealed by passwd); new contract contracts/drivers/contract_p4_keyquorum.h (P4-9, drivers REV 5); the fl_kq_driver_t ops over the KeyQuorum kq_file_* C ABI (kernel/drivers/keyquorum/kq_driver.c); the checkpoint orchestrator kernel/core/vfs/kq_checkpoint.c; the host store kernel/core/vfs/kq_delivery.c (SQLite, user_version 1, owner-only letters); session opcodes 0x39-0x3F with hooks in net_server and net_client (kernel/core/net/net_kq_delivery.c). Tests: test_mem_asm, test_heritage (box keys), new test_kq_checkpoint, test_kq_delivery and test_kq_net. Docs: docs/FILE_SHARING_KEYQUORUM.md (diagram, VAE/SNN mapping, layers, commands, limits) and docs/IDENTITY_HERITAGE.md. Limits: the host is the key authority, so shells must share its account store; the browser lab and QEMU kernel do not run co-signed delivery yet.
